from pathlib import Path
import json,html
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
d=json.loads((p/'references.json').read_text())
answers=[
'Figma separates finding a reusable item from inspecting and inserting it: Assets search and library filters lead to a Details preview with provenance and “Insert instance” (refero:flow-5039; refero:screen-2e0d5f12). Canva keeps a large preview visible while options change (refero:flow-8062). MasterClass supplies compact category/filter discovery, but in a learner context (mobbin:666b7eaa-84c1-4d32-a152-9b6ae3ae9eb9). For Essentials, combine searchable institutional/own libraries with optional scenario inspection and a persistent selection basket. Competency, duration and equipment filters are proposed domain adaptations, not demonstrated together by this set.',
'Teachable imports checked lessons from a source course into a destination curriculum (mobbin:e8676237-6e24-4e98-90a2-e37bfa82f60a). PandaDoc makes batch scope explicit with “Add 2 items” and confirms insertion in the document (mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c). Canva offers a single-design “Copy to course” / “Move” choice (mobbin:4fb0fdd5-431c-4702-9bb5-fbcb4d78c2df). Circle’s one-question authoring flow is a counterexample for this reuse task (mobbin:327fbad0-5e87-48c9-b7cf-fb0f5bcce035). Essentials should let instructors select several known scenarios, review a count, and add them once into a chosen section.',
'Figma visibly inserts a library instance, identifies its source and offers a variable-mode choice (refero:flow-5040). Ditto explicitly attaches selected text to a named library component and confirms the relationship (mobbin:9d28e0e2-ba12-4eb5-9a77-c3227f36b647). Notion exposes “Synced block,” while Canva shows a choose-and-edit handoff; neither capture establishes later synchronization (mobbin:b8778e0e-13d3-49a6-9f01-3680ea66249b; refero:flow-8062-q3). None of these captures verifies master-update propagation or override survival. Essentials needs an explicit decision on linked version, pinned copy and course-only settings before choosing interaction copy.',
'Circle supplies direct before/after evidence of moving a whole section while preserving its lessons and Draft labels (mobbin:0489e85e-877c-41fc-92dc-6e6e7bc9c7da). Kajabi makes grouped content and Draft/Publish/Drip/Lock states visible; Podia shows a delayed section; Teachable exposes date- or enrollment-based section release (mobbin:5b4497cf-d3c9-445f-bff6-754fbbb1cf7c; mobbin:0aed2e1a-0de0-4f32-9dba-2d5a627a1e87; mobbin:e84f7cdf-c9b2-4a3d-bddf-31e53e19e509). The evidence supports in-place grouping and sequence management. It does not demonstrate item-prerequisite configuration. Keep sequence distinct from event scheduling and learner release.',
'Mindvalley, MasterClass and Udemy retain activity titles, numbering and duration in learner outlines (mobbin:99d3f73c-a804-4e4d-9b11-132afbe8ab1c; mobbin:eeaba88c-51dc-44b0-8c15-cf8775b9c361; mobbin:987d1aea-1d31-4f63-ae58-5989ee6837c7). These support a scannable outline, but they do not show metadata being copied by an instructor from a master library. For Essentials, duration, competencies and equipment are candidate course-row fields; their provenance, editability and learner visibility remain design decisions. Event links should lead to the Events sub-module rather than imply that adding a scenario schedules it.',
'Podia reduces first-run uncertainty with lightweight guidance and example content; Kajabi shows an editable starter outline (mobbin:6d57146d-b827-45d3-800f-d925dc03c06c; mobbin:8edcefcc-f539-46e6-a13a-d0ed44fa3308). Teachable offers outline methods and an explained empty course list (refero:screen-4f0eb823; refero:flow-9573-q6). Circle shows an empty section with inline add controls but no library route in the captured state (mobbin:5341f9e1-8516-4a2f-b941-a3ef17a2f63f). Essentials should open with “Browse scenario library,” optional suggested scenarios and clear empty/search-empty states. MasterClass’s captured no-results message coexists with an unrelated course card, making the search state ambiguous (refero:screen-75721406). Suggested items should remain editable and should not silently become scheduled learner activities.'
]
for q,a in zip(d['questions'],answers):q['answer']=a
counters={'mobbin:327fbad0-5e87-48c9-b7cf-fb0f5bcce035','refero:screen-75721406','refero:flow-9573'}
evidence={}
for f in (p/'notes').glob('Q*.matrix.json'):
 for row in json.loads(f.read_text()):
  if row.get('reference_id'):evidence[row['reference_id']]=row['evidence']
for r in d['references']:
 r['counter_example']=r['id'] in counters;r['selected']=False
 if r['id'] in evidence:r['take']=evidence[r['id']]

(p/'references.json').write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\n')
refs={r['id']:r for r in d['references']}
def cite(i):
 r=refs[i];return f'<a href="#{html.escape(i)}">{html.escape(r["app"])} · <code>{html.escape(i)}</code></a>'
def links(*ids):return '; '.join(cite(i) for i in ids)
def item(text,*ids):return '<li>'+html.escape(text)+' '+links(*ids)+'</li>'
top=[('refero:screen-2e0d5f12','Inspect preview, description and provenance before inserting.'),('mobbin:e8676237-6e24-4e98-90a2-e37bfa82f60a','The closest course-native batch-import example.'),('mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c','A selection count makes the batch commit explicit.'),('refero:flow-5040','Shows a placed library instance with source identity and configuration.'),('mobbin:0489e85e-877c-41fc-92dc-6e6e7bc9c7da','Shows whole-section reorder with child lessons preserved.'),('mobbin:99d3f73c-a804-4e4d-9b11-132afbe8ab1c','Makes time visible across program and lesson views.'),('mobbin:6d57146d-b827-45d3-800f-d925dc03c06c','Combines guidance with an editable example outline.')]
parts=['<section id="synthesis" class="synthesis" aria-label="Research synthesis"><h3>Top examples</h3><p>30 references · 12 products · Mobbin + Refero. Captured screens and preview frames are evidence of visible interaction only. Flows preserve source order but may omit intermediate steps. This is a focused sample, not a market-wide ranking. Three counter-examples flag task mismatch or an ambiguous captured state, not overall product quality.</p><ol>']
parts += [f'<li>{cite(i)} <span class="badge">{refs[i]["source"].title()}</span> — {html.escape(why)}</li>' for i,why in top]
parts+=['</ol><h3>Pattern comparison</h3><p>✓ = direct evidence for the named part of a question; partial = adjacent or incomplete evidence; ✗ = not evidenced in this capture, not a claim that the product lacks the capability. Columns cover the six questions below.</p><div class="comparison-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable product comparison"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th>']
parts += [f'<th>{q["id"]}<br>{html.escape(q["title"])}</th>' for q in d['questions']]
parts+=['</tr></thead><tbody>']
# Short, human-reviewed matrix labels; references carry the detailed supporting evidence.
cells={
'Circle':{2:('✗','One-question authoring','mobbin:327fbad0-5e87-48c9-b7cf-fb0f5bcce035'),4:('✓','Section moves with lessons','mobbin:0489e85e-877c-41fc-92dc-6e6e7bc9c7da'),6:('partial','Empty editable section','mobbin:5341f9e1-8516-4a2f-b941-a3ef17a2f63f')},
'Teachable':{1:('✗','New-course wizard','refero:flow-9573'),2:('✓','Checkbox lesson import','mobbin:e8676237-6e24-4e98-90a2-e37bfa82f60a'),4:('partial','Sections + release panel','mobbin:e84f7cdf-c9b2-4a3d-bddf-31e53e19e509'),5:('✗','Generation inputs only','refero:screen-755d46c4'),6:('✓','Outline method choice','refero:screen-4f0eb823')},
'Kajabi':{4:('partial','Grouped state badges','mobbin:5b4497cf-d3c9-445f-bff6-754fbbb1cf7c'),6:('✓','Editable starter modules','mobbin:8edcefcc-f539-46e6-a13a-d0ed44fa3308')},
'Podia':{4:('partial','Sections + delay label','mobbin:0aed2e1a-0de0-4f32-9dba-2d5a627a1e87'),6:('✓','Guidance + example content','mobbin:6d57146d-b827-45d3-800f-d925dc03c06c')},
'Figma':{1:('✓','Library filters + details','refero:flow-5039'),3:('✓','Named linked instance','refero:flow-5040')},
'Notion':{3:('partial','Synced block menu only','mobbin:b8778e0e-13d3-49a6-9f01-3680ea66249b')},
'Ditto':{3:('partial','Explicit attach + confirmation','mobbin:9d28e0e2-ba12-4eb5-9a77-c3227f36b647')},
'Canva':{1:('partial','Persistent live preview','refero:flow-8062'),2:('partial','Single design copy/move','mobbin:4fb0fdd5-431c-4702-9bb5-fbcb4d78c2df'),3:('partial','Choose/edit handoff','refero:flow-8062-q3')},
'MasterClass':{1:('partial','Learner library filters','mobbin:666b7eaa-84c1-4d32-a152-9b6ae3ae9eb9'),5:('partial','Numbered timed activities','mobbin:eeaba88c-51dc-44b0-8c15-cf8775b9c361'),6:('✗','No-results + unrelated card','refero:screen-75721406')},
'Udemy':{4:('partial','Published course hierarchy','mobbin:045c215d-6e08-432c-9bb6-3ddd4495fc69'),5:('partial','Type + remaining time','mobbin:987d1aea-1d31-4f63-ae58-5989ee6837c7')},
'Mindvalley':{5:('partial','Program/lesson durations','mobbin:99d3f73c-a804-4e4d-9b11-132afbe8ab1c')},
'PandaDoc':{2:('✓','Count-aware batch insertion','mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c')}}
for app,cs in cells.items():
 parts.append('<tr><th scope="row">'+app+'</th>')
 for q in range(1,7):
  if q in cs:
   status,label,i=cs[q];parts.append('<td>'+status+' · '+html.escape(label)+cite(i)+'</td>')
  else:parts.append('<td>✗ · Not captured</td>')
 parts.append('</tr>')
parts+=['</tbody></table></div><h3>What the best apps do differently</h3><ul>']
parts += [
item('They separate inspection from commitment. Figma exposes provenance and a precise insertion action; Canva lets alternatives change a persistent preview. For Essentials, preview can be optional while selection remains persistent.','refero:screen-2e0d5f12','refero:flow-8062'),
item('They show batch scope before committing. Teachable uses lesson/section checkboxes; PandaDoc names the selected count in its add action. Both show the inserted result, unlike the single-question creation path captured in Circle.','mobbin:e8676237-6e24-4e98-90a2-e37bfa82f60a','mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c','mobbin:327fbad0-5e87-48c9-b7cf-fb0f5bcce035'),
item('They make the reuse relationship legible. Figma names the library behind a placed instance; Ditto confirms attachment to a component. These are stronger precedents for source identity than an insertion menu alone. They still do not prove update propagation.','refero:flow-5040','mobbin:9d28e0e2-ba12-4eb5-9a77-c3227f36b647','mobbin:b8778e0e-13d3-49a6-9f01-3680ea66249b'),
item('They keep structure and status together. Circle visibly moves grouped lessons; Kajabi shows release states within the outline. Sequence and release can be managed nearby while remaining distinct concepts.','mobbin:0489e85e-877c-41fc-92dc-6e6e7bc9c7da','mobbin:5b4497cf-d3c9-445f-bff6-754fbbb1cf7c'),
item('They preserve useful planning detail in the outline. Mindvalley shows program and lesson time; Udemy puts type and remaining duration on activity rows. This supports showing simulation duration without repeatedly opening each scenario.','mobbin:99d3f73c-a804-4e4d-9b11-132afbe8ab1c','mobbin:987d1aea-1d31-4f63-ae58-5989ee6837c7'),
item('They offer a route out of an empty course. Podia combines guidance and example content; Kajabi supplies an editable structure. Circle’s captured empty scaffold makes the next manual action visible but gives no library-discovery route.','mobbin:6d57146d-b827-45d3-800f-d925dc03c06c','mobbin:8edcefcc-f539-46e6-a13a-d0ed44fa3308','mobbin:5341f9e1-8516-4a2f-b941-a3ef17a2f63f')]
parts+=['</ul><h3>Best practices top companies converge on</h3><p>Actionable recommendations inferred from the named examples in this sample; they are not claims of universal industry consensus.</p><ul>']
parts += [item('Provide search, source context and an optional detailed preview before adding.','refero:flow-5039','refero:screen-2e0d5f12','mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c'),item('Persist multi-selection, show its count, commit once and confirm the destination result.','mobbin:e8676237-6e24-4e98-90a2-e37bfa82f60a','mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c'),item('Keep grouping and add controls in the course outline, with visible item/release states.','mobbin:0489e85e-877c-41fc-92dc-6e6e7bc9c7da','mobbin:5b4497cf-d3c9-445f-bff6-754fbbb1cf7c','mobbin:e84f7cdf-c9b2-4a3d-bddf-31e53e19e509'),item('Show activity duration and type where instructors review the sequence; verify instructor and learner metadata separately.','mobbin:99d3f73c-a804-4e4d-9b11-132afbe8ab1c','mobbin:987d1aea-1d31-4f63-ae58-5989ee6837c7'),item('Offer an editable starting structure and lightweight guidance, with the reusable library as Essentials’ primary entry action.','mobbin:6d57146d-b827-45d3-800f-d925dc03c06c','mobbin:8edcefcc-f539-46e6-a13a-d0ed44fa3308')]
parts+=['</ul><h3>Open questions for Essentials 2.0</h3><p>These are product decisions prompted by gaps in the captured evidence, not inferred platform behavior.</p><ul>']
parts += [item('Does adding a scenario pin a version, create a copy, or link to a live master? Which course-only settings survive updates, and who approves those updates? Figma and Ditto make identity visible but do not settle propagation.','refero:flow-5040','mobbin:9d28e0e2-ba12-4eb5-9a77-c3227f36b647'),item('How should duplicate scenarios, unavailable institutional items and partial batch failures behave? The successful Teachable/PandaDoc captures do not establish these cases.','mobbin:e8676237-6e24-4e98-90a2-e37bfa82f60a','mobbin:7833133c-7d81-4179-86a5-6ba8ce80b92c'),item('Which metadata belongs to the scenario master, which can be overridden for the course, and which is safe to show in the Learner Portal? Duration is evidenced; competency mappings and equipment carry-through are not.','mobbin:99d3f73c-a804-4e4d-9b11-132afbe8ab1c','mobbin:eeaba88c-51dc-44b0-8c15-cf8775b9c361'),item('Does course sequence constrain event order or prerequisites, and does adding a scenario create any event at all? Circle demonstrates outline order; Teachable demonstrates release timing. Neither proves a simulation scheduling relationship.','mobbin:0489e85e-877c-41fc-92dc-6e6e7bc9c7da','mobbin:e84f7cdf-c9b2-4a3d-bddf-31e53e19e509'),item('What reaches Canvas and the Learner Portal: a versioned scenario link, an activity shell, or only event-facing information? The learner outlines show useful hierarchy but no Canvas hand-off or instructor-only debrief separation.','mobbin:045c215d-6e08-432c-9bb6-3ddd4495fc69','mobbin:987d1aea-1d31-4f63-ae58-5989ee6837c7')]
parts+=['</ul><p class="muted">Coverage limits: this search did not return usable direct Canvas/Moodle scenario-library evidence. Generic library patterns and learner-facing analogues are labeled throughout. All selections remain false for the later converge pass.</p></section>']
